    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "An artist had $x$ litres of red paint and $y$ litres of blue paint. In order to spray her sculpture in purple, she mixed $\\frac{1}{18}$ of the red paint with $\\frac{6}{35}$ of the blue paint. How much purple paint did she produce?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(\\frac{x}{18}+\\frac{6y}{35}\\right)\\text{ L}$",
      "worked": "Red paint used: $\\frac{1}{18}\\times\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{x}{18}$ litres.\n\nBlue paint used: $\\frac{6}{35}\\times\\frac{y}{1}=\\frac{6y}{35}$ litres.\n\nAdding the two volumes gives $\\left(\\frac{x}{18}+\\frac{6y}{35}\\right)$ litres of purple paint.",
